{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792171955,"nonce":"I1x5xud4zBT0iKHLaOBIRuKl4TQ=","message":"Fixed in cff313d (picking up Blinc git-bug f1a93f8 / blinc_abi dea3919): break_lines in blinc_text now gives half a pixel of tolerance against max_width, since Taffy's round-to-nearest layout rounding can take a label's own box up to half a pixel under its true shaped width. TextWrapRounding (tests/fixtures/components) reproduces the exact reported pattern (wrapping depends only on string+size, nothing else on screen) and confirms both the break and the fix: reverting the epsilon locally reproduces 6 of 12 cases wrapping, matching the reported shape exactly; with the fix, 12/12 pass. Thanks to chimpmonk-be for building the isolated repro that found the real mechanism — the apostrophe and cross-size-cache theories were both red herrings.","files":null}]}